(2. Vehicle intrusion during live traffic interface [High -> Medium]) Tj
T*
(   Those at risk: Site workers, road users) Tj
T*
(   Initial: L4 x S5 | Residual: L2 x S3) Tj
T*
(   Controls: Implement temporary traffic management with cones and barriers. Use traffic) Tj
T*
(management operatives. Ensure high-visibility clothing and work zone lighting.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(3. Public interference with work areas [High -> Low]) Tj
T*
(   Those at risk: Site workers, public) Tj
T*
(   Initial: L3 x S4 | Residual: L2 x S2) Tj
T*
(   Controls: Use barriers, signage, and controlled access points. Maintain safe) Tj
T*
(pedestrian routes. Use a marshal where public interaction cannot be segregated.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(4. Contact with overhead services [High -> Medium]) Tj
T*
(   Those at risk: Site workers using machinery) Tj
T*
(   Initial: L3 x S5 | Residual: L2 x S3) Tj
T*
(   Controls: Identify overhead services and confirm exclusion distances. Use goalposts) Tj
T*
(and height restrictors. Employ a spotter during operations.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(5. Dust exposure [Medium -> Low]) Tj
T*
(   Those at risk: Site workers, nearby residents) Tj
T*
(   Initial: L3 x S3 | Residual: L1 x S2) Tj
T*
(   Controls: Use water suppression and RPE. Segregate dusty work areas and clean using) Tj
T*
(wet methods.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(6. Noise and vibration exposure [Medium -> Low]) Tj
T*
(   Those at risk: Site workers) Tj
T*
(   Initial: L3 x S4 | Residual: L1 x S2) Tj
T*
(   Controls: Assess HAVS and noise exposure, limit trigger time. Use low-vibration) Tj
T*
(tools, rotate tasks, and provide hearing protection.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(7. Collision between plant and pedestrians [High -> Medium]) Tj
T*
(   Those at risk: Site workers, pedestrians) Tj
T*
(   Initial: L4 x S5 | Residual: L2 x S3) Tj
T*
(   Controls: Use exclusion zones with barriers. Assign a banksman for guiding plant) Tj
T*
(movements. Ensure plant pre-use checks.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(8. Excavation collapse [High -> Low]) Tj
T*
(   Those at risk: Site workers) Tj
T*
(   Initial: L3 x S5 | Residual: L1 x S3) Tj
T*
(   Controls: Assess ground conditions, use shoring as needed. Keep spoil away from) Tj
T*
(edges. Provide edge protection and inspect after weather events.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(METHOD STATEMENT) Tj
T*
(----------------) Tj
T*
(1. Review site plans and perform CAT scans. 2. Set up safe zones and traffic management. 3.) Tj
T*
(Conduct site induction specific to the project. 4. Begin excavation using hand tools near) Tj
T*
(identified services. 5. Use compact excavator to remove soil. 6. Expose and repair duct. 7.) Tj
T*
(Refill trench with granular sub-base and compact. 8. Restore area and remove site equipment.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(PPE) Tj
T*
(---) Tj
T*
(High-visibility clothing, Hard hats, Safety boots, Gloves, Hearing protection, Dust masks) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
